  "description": "Bridgey Protocol v1 golden vectors. Android (ProtocolGoldenVectorsTest) and macOS (ProtocolGoldenVectorsTests) decode every vector and must reach the same result. Frames: 'line' is one frame without its line ending (LF unless 'lineEnding' says otherwise); 'lineBase64' gives raw bytes; 'nest': N builds {\"kind\":\"x.y\",\"sessionId\":S,\"x\":[[...]]} nested N deep (the outer object counts as 1); 'padTo': N builds a pairing.offer whose deviceName is 'a' repeated until the frame is N bytes, and '@PAD@' in 'expect' stands for that name. Payloads: 'plaintext' is serialized by each platform's own JSON encoder; 'plaintextString' is used byte for byte. 'reject', 'invalid' and 'ignored' are the documented outcomes; see docs/protocol.md.",
